## Development guards

{{DEVELOPMENT_GUARDS}}

Development work uses a private fingerprinted request/result record, respects the selected workspace policy, runs declared evaluations in fresh expectation-withheld workers, and never treats a generated projection or passing self-report as canonical authority.

Before following a selected development workflow, call `soter_create_development_request` with its exact target set and the smallest requested local-effect subset. Core derives the current realized host, active configuration and lock, and target fingerprints without requiring pre-request file reads. Continue only from a current returned request boundary; `soter_inspect_development_run` reports sanitized current, stale, or closed state and grants no new authority.

Use Soter Core for resolution, policy, approval, durable checkpoints, recovery, and inspection. Host-native tool names and provider content do not redefine Automation or Context contracts. A local projection does not establish host launch, tool discovery, authentication, provider reachability, connected behavior, or health.
